# s2b-model-proxy-relay -> CORE-WIRE-G2 (lead applies, then deletes this file)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-connections/Cargo.toml

`[dependencies]`, after `mixdog-protocol = { workspace = true }`:

    mixdog-app-protocol = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-app-server-client = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
    async-trait = { workspace = true }
    serde = { workspace = true }
    serde_json = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "macros"] }
    tokio-util = { workspace = true }

New `[dev-dependencies]` section (or merge with the one other s2b tasks add), after `[dependencies]`:

    [dev-dependencies]
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "sync", "macros", "time", "test-util"] }

(`mixdog-app-server-client` has no dependency on `mixdog-connections`: no cycle. `mixdog-connections` is not yet a workspace
member, see deferred-g1.md; the edges and `cargo update --workspace --offline` + `cargo hakari generate` go in with it.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-connections/src/lib.rs

`pub mod model_proxy_relay;` is already declared. Nothing to add.

## Registration / SERVICE_PENDING

None: this task registers no protocol method. `model/proxy/execute` is a server request already in server_requests.rs.
The composition (the code that builds `Arc<dyn LocalModelProxy>` over `ModelProxyService::run_local` of
mixdog-core-domains `ai_admin::model_proxy_service`, calls `ModelProxyRelay::new(client, local, allowed)`, `serve()` and
`serving(bool)` per server link, and `abandon_all()`/`revoke()`) belongs to s2b-service (wave 9).
